# The build context is uploaded to the daemon in full, so this file decides
# both how fast a build starts and what could end up in an image layer.

# Secrets. .env.local in particular holds a real ENCRYPTION_KEY on a developer
# machine, and a copy of it inside an image is a copy that outlives the laptop.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile. Copying a host node_modules
# also copies platform-specific binaries — a Windows or macOS build of a native
# module inside a Linux image fails at require time, not at build time.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Regenerated in the build stage; a stale copy from the host would
# silently win over the fresh one.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo

# Generated. `prisma generate` runs in the build stage against the schema.
packages/database/generated
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.log
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
test-results

# Documentation does not affect a build, and excluding it keeps the context
# small. STATUS.md and the design docs live in the repository, not the image.
*.md
!README.md
docs
